## 3. Entity Definitions

For each entity in the system:

### Entity: [Name]

**Overview**:
- Description: What this entity represents
- Business owner: Who is responsible for the data
- Technical owner: Which service/module manages this entity
- Source of truth: This system / External system [name]
- Expected volume: Rows at launch / at 1 year / at 3 years
- Growth rate: Rows per day/month

**Fields**:

| Field | Type | Nullable | Default | Constraints | PII | Description |
|-------|------|----------|---------|-------------|-----|-------------|
| id | UUID | No | gen_random_uuid() | PK | No | Primary key |
| ... | ... | ... | ... | ... | ... | ... |
| created_at | TIMESTAMPTZ | No | now() | - | No | Record creation time |
| updated_at | TIMESTAMPTZ | No | now() | - | No | Last modification time |

**Indexes**:

| Index Name | Fields | Type | Purpose |
|-----------|--------|------|---------|
| idx_[table]_[field] | field_name | B-tree / GIN / GiST | Query pattern it optimizes |

**Constraints**:
- Unique constraints
- Check constraints
- Foreign key constraints with ON DELETE behavior

**Lifecycle / State Machine** (if applicable):
```
[state1] → [state2] → [state3]
                ↘ [state4]
```

| Transition | From | To | Trigger | Business Rule |
|-----------|------|-----|---------|--------------|
| ... | ... | ... | ... | Reference BR-XXX |

**Validation Rules**:
- Field-level validation (format, range, pattern)
- Cross-field validation
- Business rule validation (reference Business Rules Catalog)

**Audit Trail**:
- Which changes are logged
- Audit log format
- Retention period

