## 5. Data Classification & Privacy

### PII Inventory

| Entity | Field | PII Type | Classification | Encryption | Masking | Retention |
|--------|-------|----------|---------------|-----------|---------|-----------|
| User | email | Contact | Confidential | At rest | Partial in logs | Account lifetime + 30 days |
| User | name | Identity | Confidential | At rest | Full in analytics | Account lifetime + 30 days |

### Data Classification Levels

| Level | Description | Access Control | Encryption | Logging |
|-------|-----------|---------------|-----------|---------|
| Public | Non-sensitive | No restrictions | Optional | Standard |
| Internal | Business-sensitive | Role-based | At rest | Standard |
| Confidential | PII, financial | Need-to-know | At rest + field-level | Enhanced |
| Restricted | Credentials, tokens | System-only | Always encrypted | Full audit |

## 6. Data Retention & Archival

| Entity | Active Retention | Archive Period | Deletion Policy | Legal Hold | Regulation |
|--------|-----------------|---------------|----------------|-----------|-----------|
| User | Account lifetime | 30 days post-deletion | Hard delete PII, anonymize analytics | Yes | GDPR Art. 17 |
| Audit Log | 1 year | 6 years | Archive to cold storage | Yes | SOC 2 |
| ... | ... | ... | ... | ... | ... |

### Account Deletion Process
1. What data is hard-deleted
2. What data is anonymized
3. What data is retained (with legal basis)
4. Timeline for deletion completion
5. Verification process

