CRITICAL INSTRUCTIONS:
- Every entity MUST include field types, constraints, nullability, and PII classification.
- Include realistic field definitions, not just "id, name, created_at" — think about all the fields this entity actually needs.
- PII classification is mandatory for every field that stores user data.
- Retention policies must reference applicable regulations (GDPR, CCPA, etc.).
- Include the ER diagram as a Mermaid diagram with all relationships.
- Index strategy must be justified by specific query patterns.
- State machines for entities with lifecycle (orders, subscriptions, etc.) are mandatory.
- Think about what happens when a user deletes their account — document the cascade and anonymization behavior.

Format as a well-structured markdown document with Mermaid diagrams and tables.
